:-0.009137,"pass_rate":0.7027,"pass_rate_neutral":0.7021,"def_epa_per_play":-0.03091},{"week":18,"opponent":"SF","home":true,"pf":47.0,"pa":24.0,"off_snaps":63,"epa_per_play":0.2486,"pass_rate":0.5556,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6154,"def_epa_per_play":0.009233}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2022,"team":"SEA","distance":0.6551,"shared":21,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"PIT","distance":0.773,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"DEN","distance":0.8299,"shared":21,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"TEN","distance":0.8341,"shared":21,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"SEA","distance":0.8376,"shared":22,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"TEN","distance":0.8773,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"LAC","distance":0.921,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Jesse Minter"},{"season":2023,"team":"NE","distance":0.9521,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"ATL","distance":0.9623,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2021,"team":"TEN","distance":1.001,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Cardinals went 8-9 in 2024 and outscored opponents 400 to 379. The offense carried the team, ranking 11th in EPA per play while the defense finished 26th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive traits were the 2nd highest 13 personnel usage and the fewest defenders in the box in the league.","offense":"The Cardinals offense was a little above average by EPA per play. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Schematically, they stood out for the 2nd highest 13 personnel usage and the most tight ends on the field in the league. Kyler Murray ran the passing game and leaned heavily on Trey McBride, who drew 28% of the targets.","defense":"The Cardinals had one of the worst defenses in the league, ranking 26th or worse in four of the five main efficiency measures. Even its strongest area, sack rate, only ranked 14th, and it was 31st in success rate allowed. Dennis Gardeck was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Zaven Collins, who had 5 sacks despite playing only 55% of the snaps. In terms of scheme, they had the fewest defenders in the box in the league.","special":"The Cardinals were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 89% of field goals, which was well above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the secondary, about 20% of the money on the books. Their tight ends were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Kyler Murray played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 3,851 yards. Trey McBride was the clear top target with 28% of the looks and 1,146 receiving yards. James Conner handled most of the work in the backfield with 62% of the carries. On defense, Zaven Collins led the team with 5 sacks and Sean Murphy-Bunting picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Drew Petzing called the offense and Nick Rallis called the defense. Their offense looked most like the 2022 Seahawks and the 2024 Steelers. Their defense looked most like the 2023 Titans and the 2025 Chargers under Jesse Minter.","trends":"The offense went from 22nd in EPA per play in 2023 to 11th in 2024, a big step forward. The defense moved from 32nd in EPA allowed per play in 2023 to 26th in 2024, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was Cover 4 rate, which went from 19% to 4%.","notes":"Every data source is available for 2024. This season uses the newer formation labels, which group singleback, I formation and empty sets together as under center, so those older formation rates are not shown."}}